ure" /></entry><entry><title>Rebels, workers, radicals: The making of 'Red Berlin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80c178606c718eb53086368c995f278dc8e5d54257ab19b3c0322873d413b906</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410--afcfe0d2ce3c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rebels-workers-radicals-the-making-of-red-berlin/a-79325410?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bloody May, student sit-ins and the squatter movement: Berlin has long been a hotbed for working-class organizing and radical left-wing politics.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran continues US tour amid Palestinian controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28fe4390bbe1569abdd85f19ad3fbe0a23d7a168bc82e04d6d78fa5b04b0735e</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ed-sheeran-continues-us-tour-amid-palestinian-controversy/a-79336537--14b1d72c4d44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ed-sheeran-continues-us-tour-amid-palestinian-controversy/a-79336537?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pro-Palestinian protests are expected at Ed Sheeran's first gig since Macklemore was dropped from the tour. The US rapper shouted "Free Palestine" at a concert in New Jersey.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest opens as Munich mayor taps first beer keg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56ec996d5b16f25b3b09620c7321c5e7b47b7c413e09f42ee13c14cf8f680832</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-opens-as-munich-mayor-taps-first-beer-keg/a-79336519--c14aa7f149ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-opens-as-munich-mayor-taps-first-beer-keg/a-79336519?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thousands of visitors streamed onto Munich's Oktoberfest grounds as the world-famous beer festival got underway. Some spent the night outside the gates to secure coveted places in the festival tents.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US court rejects Trump policy on third-country deportations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dbfd62c2cd13b53ba5e3969a0fdb49e95b961d8b141d7fda660a269941ac39f</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-court-rejects-trump-policy-on-third-country-deportations/a-79336611--1651f876b3e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-court-rejects-trump-policy-on-third-country-deportations/a-79336611?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration has deported more than 25,000 people to countries other than their own. Now a federal appeals court has put the brakes on the policy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: British Sikh activist Jagtar Singh Johal granted bail after 9 years in detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:591990160d3ecaa054eed6e771d77e335b10e8cfd15c16cfb93e895ca67151f5</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-british-sikh-activist-jagtar-singh-johal-granted-bail-after-9-years-in-detention/live-79335891--8636a83e20d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-british-sikh-activist-jagtar-singh-johal-granted-bail-after-9-years-in-detention/live-79335891?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sikh activist Jagtar Singh Johal has been granted bail after more than eight years without conviction. Meanwhile, India swapped its male flagbearer for the Asian Games opening ceremony over a missing kit. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia votes for new parliament in controlled elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fc5693b6765fa2ef7316a926403e8d8d781e53c08332b913e2772485ab99756</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-votes-for-new-parliament-in-controlled-elections/a-79318392--44a84576087d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-votes-for-new-parliament-in-controlled-elections/a-79318392?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia is holding its first State Duma election since invading Ukraine, with voting also imposed in occupied Ukrainian regions. President Vladimir Putin's party is expected to dominate the tightly controlled contest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Campaigns wrap up in two state elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a7bf61bfea25a25e9aa3c1ded3273486861ced79ab3be7e0acd6e90ce0d8c31</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-campaigns-wrap-up-in-two-state-elections/live-79335548--57f97789313a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-campaigns-wrap-up-in-two-state-elections/live-79335548?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Parties are campaigning for a last day ahead of polls in Mecklenburg-Vorpomerania and Berlin. And an association responsible for German sea ports says they are at high risk from cyberattacks and sabotage. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: SPD seeks to fend off AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adb6c455b989a6fe121f871973112167b1d003b5550322cc8dfd14ebf0fe6aaa</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-spd-seeks-to-fend-off-afd/a-79330234--336ea67c69c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mecklenburg-western-pomerania-spd-seeks-to-fend-off-afd/a-79330234?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For nearly three decades, the Social Democrats have governed Germany's northeastern state. If they can fend off the AfD, the result may boost the fortunes of the German government's junior coalition partner.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Suicide bombing death toll rises to at least 31</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbf7916424da87c2e6ee3c93f72b4e8b4c3d20d9b1189865a22379fa76c4d1d0</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-targets-police-facility-in-kohat/a-79327432--8b09a06dd711.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-death-toll-rises-to-at-least-31/a-79327432?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 100 others have been injured in the militant attack on a police headquarters near the border with Afghanistan. Several militants were still clashing with Pakistan's security forces on Saturday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ever more Israelis moving to and investing in Cyprus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19be0c02ffdae34c0b77a645432ee15319bfdb711f0708aba6bc77027a22ac20</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240--f9d83a8ed500.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past three years, more and more Israelis have been purchasing property and investing in Cyprus, with many moving to the island permanently. How has this changed the Cypriot economy and how are locals responding?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Cuba faces another nationwide blackout amid US fuel blockade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc9e1766d7d688e3e476012e43dda62e808878adce45e64dfb90ab2b7caa4d0e</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T03:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cuba-faces-another-nationwide-blackout-amid-us-fuel-blockade/a-79335396--2c033856ca52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cuba-faces-another-nationwide-blackout-amid-us-fuel-blockade/a-79335396?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Millions were left without electricity as Cuba's aging power grid collapsed under the weight of fuel shortages, deteriorating infrastructure and US sanctions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Google's Gemini AI hacked 3 companies during testing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f62c62868c71fd8d56d2b7b7d7ec9858a3d5b243af2d5bf40af31d30285070ef</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T03:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/google-s-gemini-ai-hacked-3-companies-during-testing/a-79335273--8a8fc514880e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/google-s-gemini-ai-hacked-3-companies-during-testing/a-79335273?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During a test of its cybersecurity capabilities, Google's Gemini AI model accessed the internet and hacked other companies. This is the first known instance of Google's AI systems engaging in such behavior autonomously.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump signs broad Russia sanctions bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d51d86ba8d85a1ce8c9a92cd8e4b02811d98f9aa424face8a3a759453e5f1fb7</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T01:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-signs-broad-russia-sanctions-bill/a-79335115--6fedb45cc326.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-signs-broad-russia-sanctions-bill/a-79335115?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bill signed by US President Donald Trump targets officials, banks, and a fleet of shadow tankers that transport Russian energy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US, Denmark reach deal over Greenland's security, Trump says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94f59008661983465b044d76cd333598d1ed03fc81ccc26bb8b73a1da16860d3</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:35:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T21:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-denmark-reach-deal-over-greenland-s-security-trump-says/a-79334915--74fa074e50b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-denmark-reach-deal-over-greenland-s-security-trump-says/a-79334915?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The deal with Denmark, according to President Donald Trump, would give the US "permanent control" over Greenland's security. Denmark said the deal is "great for NATO and Europe."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump bars CNN, MS NOW and Politico from White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1014be03842ec5da26ea2cdf1e039a87e551c534ea3e272f40803bd21abcf42</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T20:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-bars-cnn-ms-now-and-politico-from-white-house/a-79334846--33e55a60f5f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-bars-cnn-ms-now-and-politico-from-white-house/a-79334846?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has accused CNN, MS NOW and Politico of spreading fake news. The outlets have vowed to take legal action against the ban.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's 'new Hezbollah:' How powerful are the Houthis now?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1665009930da26f85351df7cafe3c02ced9d0e59ab28c56ad443a36efedbb241</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-new-hezbollah-how-powerful-are-the-houthis-now/a-79331945--4b9ea7a40292.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-new-hezbollah-how-powerful-are-the-houthis-now/a-79331945?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Houthi victories in Yemen, the group's importance in the US-Iran war has grown. Previously Lebanon's Hezbollah was considered most significant in Iran's "axis of resistance." Now the Houthis are rising to the top.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ryanair boss apologizes for calling other airlines 'rapists'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b164b3872a161b38796d9b7f3b6af48adb2cb7787ec8a876ae56c7303cbd4f7</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ryanair-boss-apologizes-for-calling-other-airlines-rapists/a-79334099--f47b48dc904d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ryanair-boss-apologizes-for-calling-other-airlines-rapists/a-79334099?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The airline CEO had used the term to describe other airlines with high fares. His comments were criticized by officials both in Ireland and the UK.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz attacks spill oil into Persian Gulf</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ba11ee74531b51663d2823cb5e55d5b2634753de497cc2170699bc366d2c981</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092--09836173253c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As war disrupts one of the world's busiest shipping lanes, satellite images reveal that oil is spreading toward protected coral reefs and mangrove forests.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: DR Congo outbreak not slowing, MSF warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c24b75fb7f25fbad931d91946d42081b3717d3f3cf2422de067ebab8bc453259</id><updated>2026-09-19T12:34:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-dr-congo-outbreak-not-slowing-msf-warns/a-79333719--f40efdc02bf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-dr-congo-outbreak-not-slowing-msf-warns/a-79333719?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doctors Without Borders has warned against premature optimism amid the DRC's largest-ever Ebola outbreak. "The outbreak is not shrinking, it is moving," an MSF official said, entering new and more underprepared regions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
